# Sync with GitHub after changes

After finishing a code or deploy change in this project:

1. Ensure the change exists in the local git working tree (pull ECS-only fixes back if needed).
2. Commit with a concise message focused on why.
3. Push to `origin` (`main` unless on another branch).
4. Do not leave production-only patches that diverge from GitHub (especially `services/api` and `tools/oral_coach`).

If push cannot complete (network/auth), report the blocker and leave files ready to commit.
